  "scope": "Derive repeated-block positivity directly",
  "validation": "Paired target and all three direct client builds pass. Target and CyclicWord objects differ; MaskConstants and WindowBits objects are identical. Sixteen object-pinned probes show the target and CyclicWord printed declarations, types, axioms and sampled global simp/instance registrations match. Five unchanged external direct providers match successful source-current producer receipts.",
  "limitations": [
    "Paired clients and direct provider receipts do not establish a source-current transitive closure; wider downstream clients were not rebuilt.",
    "The recorded workspace source path for the target imported by clients was sampled before the source commit, so its hash is the baseline in both phases; the final client object was built with the separately pinned final target object.",
    "Declaration reports and sampled registrations do not establish equality of proof bodies or all persistent extensions. CyclicWord objects differ, and both phase logs have the same pre-existing warning.",
    "Compiled objects are excluded. Recorded build and probe paths refer to the original environment; full replay requires external object dependencies."
  ],
